Tara the Barbarian was cruising along with Vorpal Blade (how I got it
is a funny story all to itself, more later), waiting to find that last
potion of gain level so I could be ready for the quest.  Deep in the
dungeon I stupidly fall into a trap door that a monster just created
with a wand of digging, and fall below the Medusa level into the mazes
before the castle.  After a near-death encounter with a minotaur, I
manage to climb out of the maze.  See a green @ in front of me, think,
"Oh, an elf or something" and stupidly hit it.  Of course, it was the
Medusa... ONE turn spent putting on a blindfold would have saved me. 
AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAARGH...

Just needed to get that out of my system.  Now for the funny bit...
infected with teleportitis (no control), I bounce into a shop infested
with monsters.  HP getting low, I pray, and my god crowns me the Envoy
of Balance.  An object appears at my feet, and suddenly I find I have
sold blessed rustproof Vorpal Blade to the shopkeeper for 312 lousy
zorkmids!!!  Angered (and yet amused) beyond belief, I pick it up
(ignoring the fact that it will cost me $3450, which I don't have) and
behead everything in the store (except the shopkeeper).  My
teleportitis then kicks in, bouncing me out of the store, and a swarm
of Keystone Kops come after me.  So does the shopkeeper.  I manage to
escape and raise enough money to pay him back, but by the time I get
back to that level I realize it would probably be better just to kill
him, which with a well-timed prayer I managed to do.  (Does anyone know
if paying him would have mollified him, or was I right to just kill him
outright?)

Sigh.  This was my first go with a barbarian - I usually play less
hack-and-slash types.  Having an intelligence of 7 was not fun,
especially as my god kept granting me spellbooks that I could read but
had little chance of using.  A mind-flayer got my int down to 3 at one
point, and a blessed unicorn horn (applied several times) and potion of
restore ability would only raise it back to 6 - are mind-flayer attacks
more permanent now or something?



- Julie (and I died with a tin of tengu meat too...)


